  "description": "This walk takes you from the RSPB's Bempton Cliffs to the popular town of Bridlington. The route runs for just under 11 miles passing along the England Coast Path. Along the way there are some splendid cliff top sea views and an abundance of wildlife to look out for. Route highlights include the wonderful Flamborough Head and the peaceful woodland trails at Dane's Dyke near Bridlington.",
